From e93e7abc1a9c262ccf6d8ee895ad06f525be52f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:07:38 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] kcm_nighttime: schedule first, map on a sub-page,
 position service created after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Config keys (nighttimesettings.kcfg), the schedule preview, validator and the
KNightTime code are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- State first: the sun path chart (sunrise/sunset times) stays on top, with one small line "Night Light and dynamic
  wallpapers follow this schedule." (was a centred paragraph above everything). (HIG-001/005)
- Page is now KCM.SimpleKCM + Kirigami.FormLayout (was the newer Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry). "Determine
  sunrise and sunset times" combo box is a radio pair "Sunrise and sunset: Based on device's location / Custom times"
  (two short exclusive options, page-design section 3). Same setting "source".
- Section "Location" (noun): "Use automatic location" -> "Detect automatically", with the service note under it
  (shown once the service is known); "Use manual location:" -> "Enter coordinates" with an indented Latitude/Longitude row
  (disabled, not hidden, while Detect is chosen); the world map is a sub-page: button "Choose on Map…"
  -> kcm.push("MapPage.qml") (titled "Choose Location"). Section "Times" (custom times): Sunrise, Sunset, Transition
  duration, unchanged wording. Only the section of the chosen source is shown (alternatives, not dependent options).
- Lat/long fields got Accessible.name. Nothing removed; ia/duplicates.md: nothing to link (Night Light links here from
  its own page).
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_nighttime.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 11 rows ok, 0 lost.
- HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-057 (noun sections), page-design sections 2, 3, 7.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured):
- main.qml created the WorldMap (ShadowedRectangle, Flickable, a 148 KB worldmap.png decoded by a synchronous Image,
  zoom buttons, attribution TextEdit) and a PositionSource up front, even for the "custom times" source (the map was
  only `visible: false`). Creating a PositionSource loads the Qt Positioning backend plugin (GeoClue2) on the GUI thread
  in componentComplete.
- Now: the map exists only on the sub-page and its Image is asynchronous; the PositionSource sits in a Loader that is
  active only for "location + automatic", and only one event-loop turn after the first frame (positionAllowed Timer).
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: kcm.push(url, {positionSource: <object>}) passing a QObject from a Loader item; the schedule
preview gets an invalid QGeoCoordinate (as before for an inactive source) until the position arrives; Layout.maximumWidth
hint label inside FormLayout (16 gridUnits) as in kcm_clock 56095d1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
